cellPad: run the SDL gamepad layer on one dedicated thread, so a controller plugged in after start is seen.

SDL's joystick hotplug (IOKit/HIDAPI on macOS) is delivered through the run loop of the thread that initialised the
subsystem, and only that thread's SDL_GameControllerUpdate drains it. cellPadInit and the cellPadGetData polls come from
guest threads, so devices present at start were opened but later ones never appeared. The SDL thread now initialises SDL,
sweeps every 2 ms and keeps a snapshot; guest calls only copy it.

